    "case_id": "577",
    "case_summary": "A 61-year-old woman presented with worsening dyspnea over the previous six months, with acute exacerbation. Symptoms included dyspnea on exertion, 2-pillow orthopnea, fatigue, dry cough, and bilateral lower limb swelling worse in evenings. One episode of lightheadedness occurred a week before presentation. Medical history included a 20-year history of autoimmune condition with joint involvement, complicated by usual interstitial pneumonia pattern interstitial lung disease four years prior and keratoconjunctivitis sicca. Patient had poor therapeutic adherence due to significant barriers to care. Previous surgeries included tonsillectomy and partial hysterectomy. Non-smoker, no alcohol use.\n\nVital signs: BP 138/86 mmHg, pulse 85/min, temperature 96.5°F (35.8°C), BMI 16.3 kg/m², respiratory rate 20/min, oxygen saturation 93% on 3L oxygen. Patient was alert but chronically ill-looking and cachectic. Normal breath sounds on auscultation, no increased work of breathing or accessory muscle use. No jugular venous distention, normal heart sounds. Pupils equal and reactive, no conjunctival injection or scleral icterus. No skin rashes, ulcerations, palpable purpura, or nodules. No palpable lymph nodes. Abdomen soft, nontender, nondistended with normal bowel sounds. Muscle tone normal, power 5/5, no cranial nerve deficits. Bilateral ulnar deviation at metacarpophalangeal joints with swan neck deformities at third and fourth fingers bilaterally. No joint swelling, warmth, or redness, but tenderness noted.\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Serum sodium: 123 mmol/L (Day 1), 136 mmol/L (Day 9)- Total protein: 116 g/L (Day 1), 69 g/L (Day 9)- Serum albumin: 41 g/L (Day 1), 40 g/L (Day 9)- Serum globulin: 21 g/L- Serum creatinine: <33.6 μmol/L- Complement C3: 0.79 g/L- Complement C4: 0.114 mg/L- Serum viscosity: 13.7 relative to H₂O (Day 1), 2.2 (Day 9)- Rheumatoid factor: >1000 kIU/L (Day 1), 464 kIU/L (Day 9)Imaging Studies:- CT angiography chest: showed pulmonary edema, no pulmonary embolism- Echocardiogram: left ventricular ejection fraction 45-50%Additional Tests:- Serum protein electrophoresis: no monoclonal protein spike- Ultrasound-guided abdominal fat pad biopsy: negative for amyloid",
